WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.220
LinguaFlow is an English tutor built around a distinction:

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:06.740
a model may know an answer without having a supporting teaching

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:10.721
reference. This walkthrough focuses on the Study freeform system.

00:00:11.533 --> 00:00:15.153
The repository contains two hundred teaching notes and one hundred

00:00:15.153 --> 00:00:18.873
seventy one English drills. Each note keeps its rule,

00:00:19.053 --> 00:00:23.633
examples, and boundaries together. Content validation and fingerprints

00:00:23.633 --> 00:00:25.832
make the index reproducible.

00:00:26.633 --> 00:00:30.613
A question and optional card become a query embedding.

00:00:31.133 --> 00:00:37.113
Postgres retrieves ten vector candidates. A heuristic reranker combines

00:00:37.113 --> 00:00:43.253
cosine similarity with normalized metadata, then sends the top five to

00:00:43.253 --> 00:00:47.892
verification. This is not B M twenty five fusion.

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:52.800
One verifier checks scope, missing context, and evidence support.

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:57.260
It selects a supplied evidence identifier; the server restores the exact

00:00:57.260 --> 00:01:00.200
source text. Supported questions get a reference.

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:04.220
Uncovered questions get a disclosure. Missing text triggers

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:05.249
clarification.

00:01:06.067 --> 00:01:09.447
Embeddings are prepared before atomic index publication.

00:01:09.827 --> 00:01:12.267
Readers check the active corpus fingerprint.

00:01:12.647 --> 00:01:16.787
In the freeform path, index and provider failures remain explicit

00:01:16.787 --> 00:01:21.127
service errors. Timeouts and bounded calls control failure behavior,

00:01:21.307 --> 00:01:24.372
without promising a production latency guarantee.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:29.720
The new evaluation compares verified and raw hybrid retrieval on one

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:34.340
hundred frozen synthetic questions. Both arms use the same two hundred

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:39.000
notes. Plans pin models, prompts, labels, and budgets.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:43.268
Offline replay reproduces scoring without new model calls.

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:47.600
Using the frozen source labels, precision improves from thirty five

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:50.260
point six percent to eighty six point four percent.

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:54.300
The AI judge's correctness score improves from three point three seven

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:59.449
to three point nine eight out of four. One baseline answer could not be graded.

00:02:00.267 --> 00:02:05.301
Local pipeline p ninety five increases from two point two two to three

00:02:05.301 --> 00:02:10.880
point two zero seconds. Verified inference costs about four dollars and

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:15.207
seven cents per thousand questions at this case mix.

00:02:15.207 --> 00:02:19.487
The entire evaluation cost about one dollar and twenty two cents,

00:02:19.487 --> 00:02:21.057
including judging.

00:02:21.867 --> 00:02:26.547
In one saved case, the verifier accepts a generic health note for the

00:02:26.547 --> 00:02:30.347
idiom under the weather. The judge also credits a disclosure that is

00:02:30.347 --> 00:02:33.367
absent. Shared models can make correlated mistakes.

00:02:33.607 --> 00:02:37.690
Frozen scores stay unchanged, with the audit alongside them.

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:41.420
The evidence demonstrates an implemented retrieval system,

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:45.360
explicit failure handling, and a reproducible comparison.

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:49.400
It does not establish learning gains or real user accuracy.

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:54.060
Human review is pending, and the expanded corpus still needs coordinated

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:55.924
production index publication.
